This product extends and depends on third-party work:

Continual Learning Bench (CL-Bench)
  Authors:  Parth Asawa et al.
  Source:   https://github.com/pgasawa/continual-learning-bench
  Paper:    "Continual Learning Bench", arXiv:2606.05661
  License:  Apache License, Version 2.0

retention-bench builds on Continual Learning Bench. It is consumed as a
pinned-commit dependency (the `cl-benchmark` package; see pyproject.toml) and
is NOT redistributed in this repository. retention-bench adapts CL-Bench's
runner, task interface, and evaluation contract via a thin adapter layer
(`retention_bench/`) and adds, as its own original contributions:

  - a hard RESET — a process-kill discontinuity across which only an on-disk
    survive-directory persists; and
  - a mechanism-agnostic system-under-test contract, under which fine-tuning,
    structural growth, notes and retrieval are all modes above one process-level
    interface. Learners themselves are not part of this repository; they connect
    through that documented contract.

